<code>assert fromIndex >= -1 ==> \forall int i; this.previousSetBit(fromIndex) < i && i <= fromIndex; !this.get(i);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert fromIndex >= -1 ==> \forall int i; this.result < i && i <= fromIndex; !this.get(i);</code>

Note: In the above assert statement, `this.result` is used to denote the return value of the `previousSetBit` method. However, since JML (Java Modeling Language) does not directly support using `\result` in the way shown, we use `this.result` as a placeholder to indicate the return value. In a proper JML specification, you would use `\result` directly. Here is the corrected version:

<code>assert fromIndex >= -1 ==> \forall int i; \result < i && i <= fromIndex; !this.get(i);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert fromIndex >= -1 ==> \forall int i; this.previousSetBit(fromIndex) < i && i <= fromIndex; !this.get(i);</code>
--------------------
